{"title":"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Completely_Solve)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Completely Solve)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two jars each contain the same number of marbles, and every marble is either blue or green. In Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> the ratio of blue to green marbles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c397d2158a13d250272dd1dc5d1e232b45fb30a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />, and the ratio of blue to green marbles in Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041f00968cc7d7a327fad99444e7b3b48c5a08ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/0510fa96a9909623c5966ad29945fabc84c704a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$95$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> green marbles in all. How many more blue marbles are in Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> than in Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/3/b339e9defcffa968fcdebdaec721000dfbcf2354.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 5\\qquad\\textbf{(B) } 10 \\qquad\\textbf{(C) }25  \\qquad\\textbf{(D) } 45  \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"389\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Our ratios are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c397d2158a13d250272dd1dc5d1e232b45fb30a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> in \\( J_1 \\) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041f00968cc7d7a327fad99444e7b3b48c5a08ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> in \\( J_2 \\).\n</p><p>We start with the equation representing the total number of marbles in both jars, where \\( x \\) is the common multiplier:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/e/abef186bfb3e4168943b374e36f05d866d7f057e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[9x + x + 8x + x = 19x\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><br />\nGiven that the total number of green marbles is 95:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/2/d32f0b92bee71f918315eee90a54db2fb36c90cc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[19x = 95\\]\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Solving for \\( x \\):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/d/6edb917ca10948552e3dc9a1cfdbcc6dc5087634.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = \\frac{95}{19} = 5\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>The difference between blue marbles in \\( J_1 \\) and \\( J_2 \\) is simply \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd14bdb3660af242a5405541508a21c3b0f9e46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9x-8x=9(5)-8(5)=45-40=$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"276\" height=\"20\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/79812fd9a09e7c6ae74dd56c36106638edc816aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ GeometryMystery\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call the number of marbles in each jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> (because the problem specifies that they each contain the same number). Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26c41275e58f4e06d320e2deca4e758f1ad6179e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"33\" /> is the number of green marbles in Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/2/ca29cd57f340578db4d88c36920cbda3ad8b1e30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"12\" height=\"33\" /> is the number of green marbles in Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/1/191badeeb3bd0bab0bdf89b9371fdcd325dc7eea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x}{9}+\\frac{x}{10}=\\frac{19x}{90}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"114\" height=\"38\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b16114c96a6f7897877855c757af18c02bc0d6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{19x}{90}=95$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/f/85fcf5d7ea99a5cec1dbeb9319d9ff06b01cf32a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=450$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" /> marbles in each jar. \n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/9/799acf2caafda136525c1dae3607c17664261cee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9x}{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"21\" height=\"38\" /> is the number of blue marbles in Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/b/2dbdc6ec89e165da1374b16d7b2bb59b500ed488.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8x}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"21\" height=\"37\" /> is the number of blue marbles in Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/f/4efbdae8b3e9d34ecbdce07bd4226512dd0cf3d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{9x}{10}-\\frac{8x}{9}=\\frac{x}{90} = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"148\" height=\"38\" /> more marbles in Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> than Jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. This means the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/79812fd9a09e7c6ae74dd56c36106638edc816aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Completely_Solve.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Completely_Solve)\">Solution 3 (Completely Solve)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Completely Solve)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/f/69fc4b9ed6d75d026557e7b06c2ed483c6ed0eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/4/cd46d9508b388af41f4e3d7f16ce41e6c18b8bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"14\" height=\"11\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b7aa611365e135f58aa09d52043ecd34855fe4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a6053907b455e0ef20a366e07f007ac4fc0eb002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, represent the amount of blue marbles in jar 1, the amount of green marbles in jar 1, the \nthe amount of blue marbles in jar 2, and the amount of green marbles in jar 2, respectively. We now have the equations, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/e/c1ef64b52fd820b63ee2d506fb6a6d5244253a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b_1}{g_1} = \\frac{9}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"56\" height=\"41\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56b261ec8f77c9ffb79ef3a2d47e6fc9aa48b1dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{b_2}{g_2} = \\frac{8}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"56\" height=\"41\" />, \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d0a89882d809bafb0328e72510a505ffbd91bb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1 + g_2 =95$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />, and \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/5/2c5a4778b0e86ee43a9363f94dbe2a8b7709bb78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 + g_1 = b_2 + g_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"130\" height=\"16\" />.\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fff60520d8fdbea008c99a883436fcaf786d0c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = 9g_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/b/8bb57de2f652da6f1fa46ab62796644f3091a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2 = 8g_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" />, we substitute that in to obtain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/1329df63b928036988022dcd221dc7e42bae850b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10g_1 = 9g_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"82\" height=\"16\" />. \nCoupled with our third equation, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f777bfa849da7952ce00962e6b5d1f91ea938d99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_1 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2d2438fd8aad6d71f1fee1367fd49052ec83b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2 = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" />. We now use this information to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/2/f22e97a2d6b3ed61259ec849da326127d043d1eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 = 405$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/6/f66f5580f0464b6441ed85e2e69c21f93f5a479e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_2 = 400$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/5/5e51338bd9f2fdcdb59921b152c0b3920f5bce26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1 - b_2 = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/79812fd9a09e7c6ae74dd56c36106638edc816aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A) } 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"28\" />.\n~Binderclips1\n</p><p>~LaTeX fixed by Starshooter11\n~Typo fixed by Little\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Writing out to ratios, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/9/c397d2158a13d250272dd1dc5d1e232b45fb30a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> in jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/1/041f00968cc7d7a327fad99444e7b3b48c5a08ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8:1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"32\" height=\"13\" /> in jar <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Since the jar must have to same amount of marbles, let's make a variable <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> for each of the ratios to be multiplied by. Now we would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5fc37caeeb6ade82e800644ebc7f69d8dd35615.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9a + a = 8b + b \\rightarrow 10a = 9b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"221\" height=\"16\" />. We can take the most obvious values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> and then scale it from there. We should be able to see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> could be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. Now remember that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/1/0510fa96a9909623c5966ad29945fabc84c704a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$95$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> green marbles or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/6/646bdfd8d0fc104f2fc94e28d6ab1565b90d5034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x(a + b) = 95$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" /> for some integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> to scale it. Substituting and dividing, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c43970aa97091f384854d477a1e1e07356887266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />. Thus to find the difference of the blue marbles we must do \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/7/03721118d76d4d335a7740cb90aa8d070184159c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} x(9a - 8b) &amp;= \\\\ 5(81 - 80) &amp;= \\\\ 5(1) &amp;= \\boxed{\\textbf{(A) }5} \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"162\" height=\"79\" />\n</p><p>~ Wiselion\n~Typo fixed by Ewiz\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/gQRZqfZBUAY\">https://youtu.be/gQRZqfZBUAY</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DzQZtQvNDwA?t=9\">https://youtu.be/DzQZtQvNDwA?t=9</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/mXvetCMMzpU\">https://youtu.be/mXvetCMMzpU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B\">2019 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2019 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=